{"id": "1d51bb7b-2ebf-4568-bedd-724a716e99bc", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Let me gather the data needed to run the DR assessment on this table — table config, backups, PITR, replication, and anything it's connected to.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_vus85JEfh1vi6EtdsKriXE", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Run Steps 0 through 6 of the dr-starting-point skill methodology against the DynamoDB table named 'dr-demo-players' in eu-central-1, account 012345678901_1. First load the dr-starting-point skill (skill_read) and follow its method exactly.",
  "context": "User wants to know if this table is protected well enough to survive (a) bad data (accidental/malicious writes, deletes) and (b) a full AWS Region failure, and where to start on DR. They named only this one table — treat it and anything connected to it by configuration (CloudFormation stack, IAM roles/policies referencing it, Lambda functions or other compute reading/writing to it, Streams, Global Tables replicas, backup plans) as the workload per Step 0. You are acting as the subagent described in the skill's 'If you delegate data gathering' section: do NOT write the final prose report. Return DATA ONLY in the row format specified in that section: layer | resource | type | Region | in-Region redundancy | backups (kind, frequency, retention) | copies/replicas outside the Region | point-in-time recovery status | replication status | what could not be read. Also explicitly report: whether the table exists as named (if not, list closest candidates in the account/region), whether it is a Global Table (replica regions), DynamoDB Streams status, PITR status (continuous backups), on-demand backup list, any AWS Backup plan/vault coverage and whether cross-Region copies actually exist yet (not just configured), table billing mode, and any CloudFormation stack or tags indicating a broader workload.",
  "resources": ["dynamodb table dr-demo-players", "region eu-central-1", "account 012345678901_1"],
  "timeframe": "current state as of now",
  "criteria": "Read-only checks only. Follow Steps 0-6 of dr-starting-point. Return the data rows plus the Step 7 outline handoff line as instructed by the skill for subagents. Do not write the final answer."
}", "deep_research": true}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Gather DynamoDB table and connected resource data for a DR readiness check in eu-central-1."}], "created_at": null}
